    "name": "smart-git-commit",
    "description": "Use this skill for ANY git operation — commits, pushes, PRs, releases, or version tagging. Triggers on: \"commit\", \"push\", \"save my changes\", \"create a PR\", \"open a pull request\", \"ship this\", \"make a release\", \"tag this version\", \"checkpoint my work\", or any request to record or publish code changes. Produces gold-standard commits using a unique 5-part format (CONTEXT/CHANGE/WHY/IMPACT) that is more useful and human-readable than any other agent's default git behavior. Includes secret scanning, test gating, atomic splitting, issue linking, PR creation, and release tagging. Use aggressively whenever git is involved.\n",
